  "question": {
    "text": "Let $\\alpha, \\beta \\in \\mathbf{R}$. Let the mean and the variance of 6 observations $-3,4,7,-6, \\alpha, \\beta$ be 2 and 23 , respectively. The mean deviation about the mean of these 6 observations is :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "mm3kP",
      "text": "$\\frac{13}{3}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "cuRC1",
      "text": "$\\frac{16}{3}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "w1tHR",
      "text": "$\\frac{11}{3}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "4ucby",
      "text": "$\\frac{14}{3}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\frac{\\sum x_i}{6}=2 \\text { and } \\frac{\\sum x_i^2}{N}-\\mu^2=23 \\\\\n& \\alpha+\\beta=10 \\\\\n& \\alpha^2+\\beta^2=52\n\\end{aligned}$\nsolving we get $\\alpha=4, \\beta=6$\n$\\frac{\\sum\\left|x_i-\\bar{x}\\right|}{6}=\\frac{5+2+5+8+2+4}{6}=\\frac{13}{3}$",
    "image": null
